1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.800
Tim Hawks:

2
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:13.612
Hello gentlemen. You have made it. This is our last teaching session and next week we are going to wrap up with our celebration and get your man card. All you have to do is turn in a man plan.

3
00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:24.755
Some of you are thinking, oh, I need to do that. Yes, you need to do that. Talk to Nate, email it to Nate. And again, you know, some of you guys probably wrote a book.

4
00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:38.367
Some of you may write it on the back of your business card. As long as you got a plan, that is all we care about. And we will give you some feedback on that. But next week, we are going to celebrate that.

5
00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:50.511
Unfortunately, I am not going to be able to be here for this. I am speaking at a conference in Orlando and just not going to be able to be here. So, but our team is going to be here.

6
00:00:50.511 --> 00:00:58.451
Nate is going to be here and we really want to celebrate this. So, make sure you come. You have made it this far. Okay?

7
00:00:58.451 --> 00:01:11.997
You look around the room and you kind of look at the other guys that have fallen along the way and you are still here and you are still pushing forward and that is kind of the way it is in life with men.

8
00:01:11.997 --> 00:01:20.605
You know the follow through, the reject passivity, accept responsibility, lead courageously, that herd kind of narrows over time.

9
00:01:20.605 --> 00:01:27.745
And so that is a big challenge for us is to call the rest of the men to step up and own this manhood thing.

10
00:01:27.745 --> 00:01:36.219
Today we are going to talk about work and so the title is leaving a legacy. But I just want to challenge you guys on something.

11
00:01:36.219 --> 00:01:46.628
A number of years ago I was sitting in a group of men and I asked them the question what is your greatest legacy? And to a man they all said their children.

12
00:01:46.628 --> 00:01:56.370
Now, there is nothing wrong with that because part of our responsibility as men would be to leave the next generation, foster the next generation.

13
00:01:56.370 --> 00:02:05.445
But it was interesting to a man, everybody said, my greatest legacy is going to be my kids. Now, here is what is interesting about that.

14
00:02:05.445 --> 00:02:20.058
You have got about 18 direct years with your children before they kind of leave your direct supervision. Unless of course you have got kind of delayed adulthood and then it could be another 10 or 15 or 20 years for you.

15
00:02:20.058 --> 00:02:33.337
But typically you have got about 18 direct years but the average man will put about 45 years of their life between 40 and 50 hours a week five to six days a week of their life into some kind of work.

16
00:02:33.337 --> 00:02:42.145
And one of the questions you have to ask yourself is, is there something about what I do every day that goes beyond the utilitarian?

17
00:02:42.145 --> 00:02:52.221
Make a name for myself, make a place for myself, show off my skills, make enough money to live on, enough money to retire with. What is that all about?

18
00:02:52.221 --> 00:03:04.299
If you are a student here today, the same question is all you are doing in school is just learning to prepare yourself to get a college degree so you can work the rest of your life.

19
00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:14.842
And that is just kind of ancillary to who you are and what you do. And what I want to challenge you guys today is to think a little bit differently than that.

20
00:03:14.842 --> 00:03:50.876
So, as we start out today, suppose you were driving to work and the Balcones Fault line finally gave way and you were swallowed up in an earthquake and died and immediately you find yourself in heaven face to face with Jesus and you know, you are there and since in heaven it is timeless like one day is like a thousand years, a thousand years go by at least that is what it feels like to you just in the bliss and joy of heaven and seeing all the people that are there and celebrating what God has done and all of a sudden it dawns on you.

21
00:03:50.876 --> 00:04:04.822
I wonder what is happening back down there. And so you ask God to open up a window so you can see down there. And he opens up the window. You look down there and what you see is only a couple days have passed.

22
00:04:04.822 --> 00:04:18.434
It is your memorial service and there is everybody sitting there in your memorial service and the first thing you look for is you see your wife and she is crying and you are thinking that is a good thing.

23
00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:31.913
If she was dancing around that would not be good. You know, your wife and kids are crying. That is kind of a good thing. And then the pastor does something that we never do at Hill Country Bible Church.

24
00:04:31.913 --> 00:04:36.717
He opens up the mic for anybody in the room that wants to say something.

25
00:04:36.717 --> 00:04:51.063
The reason why I never do that is because I have no idea what skeletons you guys may have in your closet and a memorial service is not the right time to expose those though I have been in some where it has happened.

26
00:04:51.063 --> 00:05:02.073
Ouch. So, some other church pastor says, hey, we are opening a mic here. And all of a sudden you see a guy walking to the front that you had not seen in a long time.

27
00:05:02.073 --> 00:05:09.480
In fact, he was a guy that worked with you in your first job and you think, I am surprised he is at my funeral.

28
00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:18.688
And he walks up to the mic and he stops and he says, you know, 25 years ago when you came to that place of work, his life changed forever.

29
00:05:18.688 --> 00:05:32.768
And he recalls the time when he was sitting in his office having gotten the call from his wife after she caught him doing something he was not supposed to do and she had called him that day and said, it is over.

30
00:05:32.768 --> 00:05:44.645
I am done with you. That is the end of our marriage. And you walked into his office and you saw him and you looked in his face and you said, you look kind of down. What is wrong?

31
00:05:44.645 --> 00:05:55.989
And he went on and relayed to you what was going on in his marriage. And you said to him, listen, why do you not come over to the house tonight? Just come over the house.

32
00:05:55.989 --> 00:06:09.668
My wife and I would like to talk to you because we went through some hard things in our marriage, too. And I just want to give you a place to get away from it. Get a hot cooked meal and let us talk to you.

33
00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:23.614
And he says, you know, you brought me into your home and at the lowest point when nobody wanted to talk to me. Everybody was against me. And you sat me down and you talked about how God can restore a marriage.

34
00:06:23.614 --> 00:06:32.622
And you asked me, would my wife be willing to come and have dinner? And so I asked her and she said yes. And so you brought us back in.

35
00:06:32.622 --> 00:06:49.104
And we sat down and you guys began to talk about how you went through problems and you went through struggles in your marriage and how God had really helped you and you hooked them up with a counselor at your church and that counselor helped them.

36
00:06:49.104 --> 00:07:02.516
And he says, when you came into my life 25 years ago because you took the time at work to pay attention to me and took a personal interest and brought me home and worked with me, my marriage was saved.

37
00:07:02.516 --> 00:07:16.729
And just two years ago, I had the privilege of walking my daughter down the aisle to give her away in marriage, which would have never happened had things gone the way they were going before you came into my life.

38
00:07:16.729 --> 00:07:17.596
He sits down.

39
00:07:17.596 --> 00:07:31.475
A woman comes to the microphone and she says, yeah, when I went through breast cancer, I did not know what I was going to do. And you stuck your head in my office door every day and said, how you doing today?

40
00:07:31.475 --> 00:07:45.955
And my wife and I are praying for you. And she said, I went through the surgery. I went through the treatments. She said, there were days when I did not even hardly feel like I could get out of bed, but you know what?

41
00:07:45.955 --> 00:07:59.034
I got up and came to work. And the reason why I came to work is because I knew that I would see your smiling face to let me know that you were praying for me. And that is what got me through this.

42
00:07:59.034 --> 00:08:07.308
I believe because if you could believe that God would answer prayer and you were so faithful that I could trust him as well.

43
00:08:07.308 --> 00:08:19.986
Another guy gets up and he is walking up there and you are thinking, oh my goodness, that guy is here because he was your nemesis. Nemesis at work all the time. Undercut you, undermined you.

44
00:08:19.986 --> 00:08:31.463
Did everything he could to get under your skin. And you are thinking, what in the world is he going to say? And he walks up to the mic and he says, I do not know about you.

45
00:08:31.463 --> 00:08:44.808
I do not know where you were getting your life from, where it was coming from, but I always respected you. Always respected you. And I do not know what made you tick, but you made an impression on me.

46
00:08:44.808 --> 00:08:56.552
The way you responded when other people took credit for your work. The way you gave a kind word in meetings when everybody else was losing control. The way you dealt with that.

47
00:08:56.552 --> 00:09:01.223
Like, I do not know where that was coming from. And he sits back down.

48
00:09:01.223 --> 00:09:13.701
And another guy walks up and he says, I can tell you where that was coming from. One day after work, we were walking across the parking lot and you turn to me and you asked me a question.

49
00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:22.976
And you said, this may feel a little personal to you, but I just wonder, do you have any idea what is going to happen to you after you die?

50
00:09:22.976 --> 00:09:37.189
Like, if you died today, do you have any idea whether you would go to heaven or whether you would go to hell? And I thought when you said that, you cannot ask me that question. You cannot. That is not appropriate.

51
00:09:37.189 --> 00:09:47.665
Like, we are walking across the parking lot at work. You cannot ask me that question. And so, I just kind of brushed you off, but it bugged me. It bugged me.

52
00:09:47.665 --> 00:09:59.943
I laid in bed at night and I wondered about that question and it was driving me crazy. And so I came back to you and I asked you like what did that mean? And you started talking to me.

53
00:09:59.943 --> 00:10:12.154
We started talking about faith issues and about God issues. And I did not know anything about it. I went to Sunday school a few times when I was a kid. I did not really have any idea.

54
00:10:12.154 --> 00:10:20.561
And over the course of a couple months through our dialogue, I began to understand who Jesus was and what he did on my behalf.

55
00:10:20.561 --> 00:10:32.705
And I put my faith in Jesus Christ and I came to faith and I led my wife to faith and my kids all came to faith and we are all walking with Jesus today. We are plugged into a church.

56
00:10:32.705 --> 00:10:42.914
We are doing ministry together and I am looking forward to seeing you again because I have confidence I am going to be in heaven because of what you did.

57
00:10:42.914 --> 00:10:54.324
Would that happen at your funeral by the way you are conducting yourself and living your life in the work environment that God has placed you in? So that is the challenge.

58
00:10:54.324 --> 00:11:02.665
Do you leave an eternal legacy through all the time and energy you invest over the course of your life living your work life?

59
00:11:02.665 --> 00:11:18.479
Today I want to just challenge us on how to imagine that and then how to move it into reality as a man who has been called to a transcendent cause to change the world through the way you do life day by day in your personal relationships.

60
00:11:18.479 --> 00:11:32.225
And we are going to follow Philippians chapter 1. So I encourage you to grab your Bibles, open it to Philippians chapter 1. If you do not have a Bible, encourage you to go online Bible Gateway or Bible app.

61
00:11:32.225 --> 00:11:39.765
You can pull up Philippians chapter 1 and follow along. We are going to be walking through this passage together.

62
00:11:39.765 --> 00:11:54.378
Really simple outline here. The first thing that we need to do to seize our opportunity as men to leave a lasting legacy through our life's work is to accept the mission. It is kind of like the Mission Impossible theme.

63
00:11:54.378 --> 00:12:03.386
Your mission if you choose to accept it. And a lot of us never choose to accept this mission. But if you will, what is going to happen?

64
00:12:03.386 --> 00:12:17.332
A couple thoughts here. Letter A. God designed work as spiritual service. God designed work as spiritual service. God did not design work for work's sake. God designed work so that we could represent him well.

65
00:12:17.332 --> 00:12:23.537
So, Adam and Eve given a job in the garden to do to represent God well and reflect his glory.

66
00:12:23.537 --> 00:12:33.746
Letter B. We are junior partners with God to establish his kingdom rule on earth. We are junior partners with God to establish his kingdom rule on earth.

67
00:12:33.746 --> 00:12:40.485
In Colossians 3:23 and 24, we will go to Philippians in just a minute, but you just write these down.

68
00:12:40.485 --> 00:12:49.493
Paul writes, "Whatever you do, work at it with all your heart as working for the Lord." In other words, your ultimate boss is the Lord.

69
00:12:49.493 --> 00:13:08.777
Your partner in what you do every day, whether it is programming a computer or building a road, your responsibility there is to work with your senior partner, who is Jesus, as working for the Lord, not for man, since you know that you will receive an inheritance from the Lord as a reward.

70
00:13:08.777 --> 00:13:19.653
It is the Lord Christ you are serving. You think you are serving the man. You think you are serving the shareholders by boosting the price of stock on Wall Street.

71
00:13:19.653 --> 00:13:29.729
You think you are serving the customer, but at the end of the day, if you are a follower of Jesus Christ, it is the Lord that you are actually serving.

72
00:13:29.729 --> 00:13:41.740
Students, you think you are serving the teacher or sometimes your parents that are kind of like, make sure you get good grades. You got to get them. They are on your case about it.

73
00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:56.287
You are actually serving Jesus in the way you go about how you learn, how you study, what you are doing on this test. It is Jesus that you are working for. Much higher motivation. And by far better retirement benefits.

74
00:13:56.287 --> 00:14:05.362
Way better retirement benefits. Do not have to worry about Social Security and what is going to happen to it. Got that covered in Jesus.

75
00:14:05.362 --> 00:14:19.442
Letter C. Therefore, our approach to work should reflect our transcendent cause of promoting God's glory, not ours. It is our transcendent cause of promoting God's glory, not ours. We are not serving the ground.

76
00:14:19.442 --> 00:14:28.650
We are not working for titles and toys. We are working for the greater cause, the cause of God's glory. It is all a matter of perspective.

77
00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:38.259
Have you accepted this mission that I work with God and for God to make a difference in the world and I do it always, including through my work.

78
00:14:38.259 --> 00:14:49.336
Two men standing in a granite quarry pounding away on a rock. You go to one side of the rock and you ask the man, what are you doing? He says, I am quarrying a stone.

79
00:14:49.336 --> 00:15:02.748
You go to the other side of the rock and you ask that man, what are you doing? He says, I am building a cathedral. What is the difference between the two? One of them sees the vision behind their work.

80
00:15:02.748 --> 00:15:16.227
The other one is just getting through the day. A nurse is emptying a bedpan and you ask her, what are you doing? Well, I am cleaning up after a patient. Another you ask the question, what are you doing?

81
00:15:16.227 --> 00:15:27.704
And she says, I am saving a life. It is all a matter of perspective. Do you have a vision that God has a mission for you at work and you are willing to accept that mission?

82
00:15:27.704 --> 00:15:35.911
Listen to what Paul says in Philippians chapter 1, starting in verse 3. He says, "I thank my God every time I remember you.

83
00:15:35.911 --> 00:15:50.124
In all my prayers for all of you, I always pray with joy because of your partnership in the gospel from the first day until now." That word partnership, koinonia, sharing our commonality. Now, wait a minute, Paul.

84
00:15:50.124 --> 00:15:54.661
You are an apostle. You are an evangelist. You are a church planter.

85
00:15:54.661 --> 00:16:08.540
And you are saying that the average folks, the Philippian jailer who works in the jail, the slaves who have come to faith there, the business owners that come, you are saying that you are a partner with them.

86
00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:17.882
I thought you had holy work and they had secular work. Paul is not saying that. What he is saying is like we are all partners in the gospel.

87
00:16:17.882 --> 00:16:32.429
I have got my role, you have got your role, but what we do, we are working together on the same team for the same cause to advance the gospel of Christ. You have got a venue to do it in. I have got a venue to do it in.

88
00:16:32.429 --> 00:16:45.174
There are places and people that I will never have a chance to talk to that you guys talk to every day. And so the partnership or the missionary work, we all share in that. That is all of us.

89
00:16:45.174 --> 00:16:57.986
One of the biggest problems that is happening in America, why we are losing ground as Christianity, is because you guys are willing to delegate the work of the gospel to the paid professional.

90
00:16:57.986 --> 00:17:10.531
And unfortunately, too many paid professionals are willing to take the pay and do it for you. And therefore, people have less and less access to the gospel unless they show up at a church.

91
00:17:10.531 --> 00:17:12.799
Was never intended to be that way.

92
00:17:12.799 --> 00:17:27.012
He says, "Being confident of this, that he who began a good work in you will carry it to completion until the day of Christ Jesus. It is right for me to feel this way about all of you since I have you in my heart.

93
00:17:27.012 --> 00:17:41.826
For whether I am in chains or defending and confirming the gospel, all of you share in God's grace with me." We all share in the same grace that has been given, we also have the same mission, our partnership in the gospel.

94
00:17:41.826 --> 00:17:47.030
"God can testify how I long for all of you with the affection of Jesus Christ.

95
00:17:47.030 --> 00:18:12.721
And this is my prayer that your love may abound more and more in knowledge and depth of insight so that you may be able to discern what is best and may be pure and blameless until the day of Christ." Now watch this phrase, "filled with the fruit of righteousness that comes through Jesus Christ to the glory and praise of God." That you would be filled with the fruit of righteousness.

96
00:18:12.721 --> 00:18:25.266
In other words, your life because of the righteousness that the gospel has birthed in you would overflow into fruit. It would make a difference in the world. Other people would be changed.

97
00:18:25.266 --> 00:18:32.339
Other people would be brought into the kingdom. That is what Paul is challenging them on to live this out.

98
00:18:32.339 --> 00:18:45.684
So accept the mission. Do you feel comfortable with terms like ambassador for Christ? I am an ambassador for Christ in the technology industry. I am an ambassador for Christ in the financial industry.

99
00:18:45.684 --> 00:19:00.097
I am an ambassador for Christ in the construction industry. I am an ambassador for Christ in the education industry. I am an ambassador for Christ in my classroom. That is what I do. I am an ambassador wherever I go.

100
00:19:00.097 --> 00:19:10.039
The fruit of righteousness, my partnership with other believers in the gospel is part of who I am, part of what I do. This is what I do with my life.

101
00:19:10.039 --> 00:19:21.650
That we are willing to accept the title missionary in college, missionary in the army barracks. I am a missionary in the restaurant business. I am a missionary wherever I go.

102
00:19:21.650 --> 00:19:34.261
I bring Christ with me and that is my mission. So the question is, has there ever been a time for you when you have said I take, Jesus, I am on board like I have signed up. This is my life.

103
00:19:34.261 --> 00:19:48.274
I am going to live it at work for you. That is who I am. If you do not adopt the mission, you will not do it. Okay, that is a man thing. Okay, I know what my job is. I know what my responsibility is. I sign up.

104
00:19:48.274 --> 00:19:49.074
I accept it.

105
00:19:49.074 --> 00:20:02.553
Once you accept the mission, the second step is to adopt the mindset. Ambassadors for Jesus Christ have a different mindset than the average person that is looking for their own gain through their work.

106
00:20:02.553 --> 00:20:15.498
Have a different mindset. First, we see the progress of the gospel, letter A, is more important than my personal progress. The progress of the gospel is more important than my personal progress.

107
00:20:15.498 --> 00:20:24.239
So, I am not primarily thinking about my advancement. I am thinking about his advancement, Jesus' advancement. Look what Paul says.

108
00:20:24.239 --> 00:20:34.315
He says, "Now, I want you to know, brothers, that what has happened to me has really served to advance the gospel." So, what has happened to you, Paul?

109
00:20:34.315 --> 00:20:42.322
"As a result, it has become clear throughout the whole palace guard and to everyone else that I am in chains for Christ.

110
00:20:42.322 --> 00:20:56.335
Because of my chains, most of the brothers in the Lord have been encouraged to speak the word of God more courageously and fearlessly." Oh, Paul, what you are saying is your personal situation, you are in jail.

111
00:20:56.335 --> 00:21:10.815
Like it does not feel like your career is working out too well. You have been imprisoned. Paul says that does not matter. It is not about my personal success. It is about the success of the cause. And Paul is chipper.

112
00:21:10.815 --> 00:21:19.022
He is giddy about his cratering career-wise because it is encouraging other people to stand up and move the gospel forward.

113
00:21:19.022 --> 00:21:22.625
I mean, the question you have to ask yourself is this.

114
00:21:22.625 --> 00:21:38.573
If today in our culture the persecution for being a visible verbal Christian, not a hidden closet Christian, a visible verbal Christian meant that tomorrow they put all pastors in lockup and chained and padlocked the doors of the churches.

115
00:21:38.573 --> 00:21:51.652
Would you become more bold? Would you become more courageous? Would you become more out there to make sure that the faith is proclaimed and the mission was carried on? Or would you go into hiding?

116
00:21:51.652 --> 00:22:01.327
Man, I do not want to lose my job. I need to keep this a secret. I do not want anybody to know. I do not want anybody to know. What would you do?

117
00:22:01.327 --> 00:22:13.471
Paul is saying, man, when the Philippians found out that Paul was in jail, they redoubled their efforts. We have lost one of our leading spokesman. We have got to get the gospel out.

118
00:22:13.471 --> 00:22:17.674
The thing that changes the world is the gospel of Jesus Christ.

119
00:22:17.674 --> 00:22:35.223
And if that first century group of people had not done that, laying the platform for the second century group of people, the third century group of people, the world, the Western world would not be Christian today because it was people in the face of persecution.

120
00:22:35.223 --> 00:22:49.636
Nero feeding people to the lions. In the face of that Christians kept sharing their faith till 20, 25 percent of the Roman Empire had converted to Christianity and it was no longer possible for them to be persecuted.

121
00:22:49.636 --> 00:23:01.914
It swept the world. It swept the world. But it swept the world because normal people were willing to continue to live out their faith and accept whatever difficulty came in their life.

122
00:23:01.914 --> 00:23:11.990
What Paul is saying is, listen, the progress of the gospel is more important than my personal progress. It is more important than my personal progress.

123
00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:24.468
He goes on to say, "It is true that some preach Christ out of envy and rivalry, others out of goodwill. The latter do so in love, knowing that I am put here for the defense of the gospel.

124
00:23:24.468 --> 00:23:40.349
The former preach Christ out of selfish ambition, not sincerely, supposing they can stir up trouble for me while I am in chains." Now, where some people are out there promoting the gospel just to cause trouble for me, what does it matter?

125
00:23:40.349 --> 00:23:54.896
"The important thing is that in every way, whether from false motives or true, Christ is preached. And because of that, I rejoice." Like as long as the gospel is going out, it really does not matter what happens to me.

126
00:23:54.896 --> 00:24:08.308
Letter B, spiritual progress of others is more important than my personal preferences. This is a mindset. The goal here is to see God glorified and the gospel go forward, not for me to get what I want.

127
00:24:08.308 --> 00:24:10.443
Notice what he says in verse 18.

128
00:24:10.443 --> 00:24:25.991
He says, "Yes, I will continue to rejoice, for I know that through your prayers and the help by the Spirit of Jesus Christ, what has happened to me will turn out for my deliverance." Oh, Paul, you think you are going to be delivered.

129
00:24:25.991 --> 00:24:27.792
What does that mean to you?

130
00:24:27.792 --> 00:24:45.341
Verse 20, "I eagerly expect and hope that I will in no way be ashamed, but will have sufficient courage so that now as always, Christ may be exalted in my body, whether by life or by death." In other words, Paul is saying deliverance for me is to get out of jail.

131
00:24:45.341 --> 00:24:58.686
And there are two ways I might go out. I might go out feet first. They might kill me. That could happen. Or I may go out head first. I may get delivered. I am expecting because you are praying for me.

132
00:24:58.686 --> 00:25:00.954
Something is going to happen here.

133
00:25:00.954 --> 00:25:10.763
Now, what is your preference, Paul? Verse 21. He says, "For me to live is Christ and to die is gain." Like what I would love to do is go to heaven.

134
00:25:10.763 --> 00:25:21.239
He says, "If I am going to go on living in the body, this will mean fruitful labor for me. Yet what shall I choose? I do not know. I am torn between the two.

135
00:25:21.239 --> 00:25:29.179
I desire to depart and be with Christ, which is better by far." Better than what? Better than what Paul has been doing.

136
00:25:29.179 --> 00:25:38.454
When you read his resume, he is living off of what he can manage by making tents to scrap together enough food so he can preach the gospel.

137
00:25:38.454 --> 00:25:50.398
Oftentimes deciding, I would rather go hungry and not work so that I can preach here so I can evangelize here so I can plant churches here. He has been shipwrecked a couple times.

138
00:25:50.398 --> 00:26:03.076
He has been beaten five times, like cat-o'-nine-tails type beating. He has been beaten with rods. He was stoned and left for dead. Like his job is a really hard job. It is a really hard job.

139
00:26:03.076 --> 00:26:15.554
It is not a cush pulpit with a great parsonage and retirement benefits. It is not that. And he is saying, man, like if Jesus calls me home, it would be a lot better to be in his presence.

140
00:26:15.554 --> 00:26:27.632
But you know, if I am going to continue to be fruitful for your sake and for the gospel's, then I need to stay. He says, "But it is more necessary for you that I remain in the body.

141
00:26:27.632 --> 00:26:44.047
Convinced of this, I know that I will remain and I will continue with all of you for your progress and joy in the faith so that through my being with you again, your joy in Christ will overflow on account of me." It is not my personal preference.

142
00:26:44.047 --> 00:26:56.058
Things are not going the way I would have designed them to go. My career is not shaping up exactly the way I would like it. But if the gospel is advancing through me, that is good.

143
00:26:56.058 --> 00:26:59.060
That is a mindset that I am willing to adopt.

144
00:26:59.060 --> 00:27:11.138
So letter A again, the progress of the gospel is more important than my personal progress. Letter B, the spiritual progress of others is more important than my personal preferences.

145
00:27:11.138 --> 00:27:23.282
And finally, the progress of the gospel comes at a personal price. Like it will cost you something if you are willing to live with a missional mindset. Look what he says in verse 27.

146
00:27:23.282 --> 00:27:29.287
He says, "Whatever happens, conduct yourselves in a manner worthy of the gospel of Christ.

147
00:27:29.287 --> 00:27:43.166
Then whether I come and see you or only hear about you in my absence, I will know that you stand firm in one spirit, contending as one man for the faith of the gospel." Standing firm, that is a military idea.

148
00:27:43.166 --> 00:27:56.511
You guys are standing shoulder to shoulder immovable and contending for, in other words, fighting against the forces of evil to ensure that every man, woman, and child in the geography where you live.

149
00:27:56.511 --> 00:28:06.320
In their case, it was a city of Philippi. That every man, woman and child have repeated opportunity just to see and hear and respond to the gospel.

150
00:28:06.320 --> 00:28:16.062
And you men are banded together, bonded together, working together as a team to evangelize your city. Now he is again he is not writing to clergy.

151
00:28:16.062 --> 00:28:22.000
He is writing to regular people who have regular jobs, regular lives, regular businesses.

152
00:28:22.000 --> 00:28:35.079
And they see themselves as this military force that day by day are taking ground to advance the gospel, not sitting on their hands. The reason why you know Jesus today is because of what they did.

153
00:28:35.079 --> 00:28:38.949
Those men picked up the banner in the face of persecution.

154
00:28:38.949 --> 00:28:47.356
He goes on to say without being frightened in any way by those who oppose you. Like most of us are afraid of an HR department.

155
00:28:47.356 --> 00:28:57.432
Most of us are afraid that if things do not go well, the debt that we have on the lifestyle that we have committed ourselves to live will not get paid.

156
00:28:57.432 --> 00:29:09.176
And tragedy of all tragedies, we end this life not to be playing golf three days a week because we can only afford two on our retirement pay. Like that is not masculine vision.

157
00:29:09.176 --> 00:29:44.809
Like what if you could lay your head down on your pillow and go off into eternity understanding that in your lifetime we ensured that every man, woman, and child in greater Austin had a repeated opportunity to see, hear, and respond to the gospel because thousands, yes, a hundred thousand men in the city invaded all the places where people show up and live their life day by day, week after week, year after year, in light of the kingdom of Jesus Christ and everybody around them knew how Jesus changed you, what he is doing in you.

158
00:29:44.809 --> 00:29:51.415
That is what Paul is saying. That is going to be hard. People are going to oppose this, oppose you.

159
00:29:51.415 --> 00:30:06.095
"This is a sign to them that they will be destroyed, but that you will be saved, and that by God, for it has been granted to you on behalf of Christ, not only to believe in him, but also to suffer for him." It is a gift.

160
00:30:06.095 --> 00:30:15.904
Facing hardship for your faith helps you identify with what Jesus did on your behalf, which takes you deeper into the experience of knowing Christ.

161
00:30:15.904 --> 00:30:27.915
Deeper into the experience of understanding love, takes you deeper into the experience of what grace means. Takes you further into that and will transform you in unbelievable ways.

162
00:30:27.915 --> 00:30:42.595
"Since you are going through the same struggles you saw I had and now you hear that I still have." Paul is not upset about his chains. He has adopted a mindset. And that mindset that he has adopted is it is not about me.

163
00:30:42.595 --> 00:30:48.400
It is not about my progress. What it is about is the gospel and it is going to be hard.

164
00:30:48.400 --> 00:30:58.342
So you accept the mission like okay God I will answer your call and I accept that it is not going to be about me. It is going to be harder than that.

165
00:30:58.342 --> 00:31:12.288
My life is going to be lived for a transcendent cause that is bigger than me at work, bigger than my family, bigger than my financial security, bigger than what we could buy, bigger than what we could acquire.

166
00:31:12.288 --> 00:31:22.631
And by the way, the millennials have adopted our materialism. Over 50 percent of millennials surveyed say becoming wealthy is a major priority for my life.

167
00:31:22.631 --> 00:31:37.244
Christian kids are no different than kids that grow up in non-Christian families. So as a man, you will always model something to the next generation. What are we modeling? Work is about wealth. Work is about lifestyle.

168
00:31:37.244 --> 00:31:40.780
Work is about personal freedom. So adopt the mindset.

169
00:31:40.780 --> 00:31:47.519
Finally, apply the method. So what does this look like at work? I mean, how do I go about doing this?

170
00:31:47.519 --> 00:32:01.932
So if you are willing to accept the mission and you start adopting the mindset, you start recognize this, adopt the mindset. What does it look like? First of all, you need to begin to pray. You need to begin to pray.

171
00:32:01.932 --> 00:32:14.410
Like the mission of God is God's business. You are his junior partner. You are just joining him in what he is already doing. And so I challenge you to begin to pray. Here is a suggestion.

172
00:32:14.410 --> 00:32:27.355
Have a marker on your way to wherever you work. Whether it is the job site, whether it is an office, whether it is working at home, have a marker somewhere along the way where you stop and pray.

173
00:32:27.355 --> 00:32:39.433
God, show up in my life today. Fill me. Reset my thinking about this day. It may be someplace along the road when you get to getting to work. It may be someplace in the parking lot.

174
00:32:39.433 --> 00:32:52.311
Like every day your ritual is when I hit this point before I hit the door, I stop and I have a conversation with God about my day. It may be the first thing you do when you get in your cubicle.

175
00:32:52.311 --> 00:33:06.791
It may be at school, the first thing you do when you get dropped off at the door or when you sit down at your desk or get to your locker. The first thing you do like that is the place. It is a sacred moment every day.

176
00:33:06.791 --> 00:33:14.398
God, get my head right. Get my heart right. Open up opportunities because you are asking God to work in your life.

177
00:33:14.398 --> 00:33:27.810
And really, our role according to scripture, three things. That we would be bold or have boldness. That we would have words. And that we would have opportunity. So, letter A, boldness. Letter B, words.

178
00:33:27.810 --> 00:33:37.419
And letter C, opportunity. Let me give you some verses that speak to this. And you might just want to write these down. I am going to read them.

179
00:33:37.419 --> 00:33:46.160
We are going to go kind of fast through this section, but I will read them to you. Here is what Paul says in Ephesians 6:19 and 20.

180
00:33:46.160 --> 00:33:58.505
He says, "Pray for me also that whenever I open my mouth, words may be given to me so that I will fearlessly make known the mystery of the gospel for which I am an ambassador in chains.

181
00:33:58.505 --> 00:34:10.783
Pray that I may declare it fearlessly as I should." So Paul is asking the Ephesian church to pray for him that he would have courage. You say, really? Like Paul was afraid. Absolutely.

182
00:34:10.783 --> 00:34:24.462
He is saying, I do not know if I have the courage to do what I am called to do in this moment, on this day, in this situation. I mean, Paul felt pain. He felt shame. He felt rebuke. He felt discouragement.

183
00:34:24.462 --> 00:34:39.009
He feels the same thing you feel. We need boldness. And Paul, the second thing Paul prays for is that I would have words that when I open my mouth, words may be given to me. You say, Paul, you wrote the book of Romans.

184
00:34:39.009 --> 00:34:51.153
Like, you are the most articulate Christian on the planet. Paul is saying, under pressure in this situation. I want God. You give me the words to say. I do not have the words to say.

185
00:34:51.153 --> 00:35:09.970
Some of you have not entered into meaningful conversations that have redemptive qualities with the people around you because you keep thinking to yourself, I do not know what to say, and if they ask me a question, I do not think I will have the answer to it, and I will look stupid.

186
00:35:09.970 --> 00:35:23.582
Well, that is again, it is about how you look. Many of us are not experiencing the supernatural move of God in our lives because we are not willing to open our mouth and watch God fill it in amazing ways.

187
00:35:23.582 --> 00:35:25.316
Paul is praying for words.

188
00:35:25.316 --> 00:35:36.459
He is also praying for opportunity. Write down Colossians 4:3-5. He says, "And pray for us too that God may open a door for our message." God, God, you open the doors.

189
00:35:36.459 --> 00:35:49.004
Open the door for our message so that we may proclaim the mystery of Christ for which I am in chains. "Pray that I may proclaim it clearly as I should." Again, Paul is praying for clarity.

190
00:35:49.004 --> 00:36:00.948
But he also says, God, open the door. Open the door. I guarantee you men, if you start praying for these things every day, okay, God, give me courage. Make me bold. Give me words.

191
00:36:00.948 --> 00:36:11.224
Like, I do not know everything, but give me words. And God, open up opportunities. You are going to start seeing opportunities come up all over the place.

192
00:36:11.224 --> 00:36:23.435
And they may be opportunities as simple as saying to somebody, how are you doing? I will pray for you. What is going on in your life? It may be opportunities that go deeper than that.

193
00:36:23.435 --> 00:36:37.314
Like, what is your spiritual background? Have you ever thought about what would happen to you when you left this life? What is your primary purpose in life? What like what drives you? What is your motivation?

194
00:36:37.314 --> 00:36:49.325
I am convinced that if you know three things about a person, you know exactly where the Holy Spirit is working in them. First one is if you know what their spiritual background is.

195
00:36:49.325 --> 00:37:01.002
So where they are coming, what their spiritual background is. Secondly, if you know what their biggest pain point is, like what is their biggest pain point? Everybody has one.

196
00:37:01.002 --> 00:37:14.214
Maybe historical something happened in the past. It may be an ongoing issue, but where their pain point is. And the third one is what is their dream? Like what is their vision? What is their desire?

197
00:37:14.214 --> 00:37:28.761
What are they living for? What is the big thing out there that really motivates them? If you know those three things, you have a place to talk deeply to them about how the gospel ministers and applies into those areas.

198
00:37:28.761 --> 00:37:32.097
So really encourage you on that. That is our role.

199
00:37:32.097 --> 00:37:46.377
But what is God's role? See, God as a senior partner is already at work. Write down John 16 verses 8-11. In John 16:8-11, Jesus tells his disciples that the Spirit of God is at work in the world to do three things.

200
00:37:46.377 --> 00:38:00.590
The first one is to convict the world of sin. Convict the world of sin. God is working in people to create the kind of guilt and conviction for their wrongdoing. The sense of morality is deeply embedded in people.

201
00:38:00.590 --> 00:38:14.136
Even if they try to reject it, it is there. Second of righteousness, the righteousness of his son. There is a moral standard. There is beauty in righteousness. There is something better than what we are.

202
00:38:14.136 --> 00:38:26.881
And our culture does everything to mask that. But in the hearts of people, the Spirit of God is working that. The final one is the Spirit convicts us of judgment to come. Of judgment to come.

203
00:38:26.881 --> 00:38:36.356
This idea that at some point in time I am going to have to give an account for the way I live my life. The Spirit of God works that in people.

204
00:38:36.356 --> 00:38:46.498
And there will be times when you talk to somebody and they will be stone-faced, uninterested. This is not going anywhere. Fine, you have planted a seed.

205
00:38:46.498 --> 00:38:57.174
There will be sometimes when you talk to people and they will interact a little bit with you and they will blow you off completely. Fine, you have watered that.

206
00:38:57.174 --> 00:39:08.785
How many people that you plant a seed with today, 10 years from now, somebody leads them to Christ, but the seed got planted with that weird guy that brought this up with me.

207
00:39:08.785 --> 00:39:33.808
And I just like, I mean the number of people that I have read about, atheists who have come to faith, many of them will say the first person that planted the challenge in my mind, I humiliated them, made them look like an idiot and they have no idea what they said to me and how that has bothered me over the last 10, 15 years until I have come to a point of accepting Jesus.

208
00:39:33.808 --> 00:39:47.153
Someday you guys are going to stand in the presence of Jesus and you are going to be meeting people that mocked you. And they are going to be walking up and thanking you for your initiation with them.

209
00:39:47.153 --> 00:39:51.557
And you are like, how did you get here? Does God let everybody in?

210
00:39:51.557 --> 00:40:05.503
And they are going to tell you the rest of the story about how God used the seed that you planted or the conversation where you watered a seed that somebody else had planted to bring them all the way to faith.

211
00:40:05.503 --> 00:40:09.306
So, we are out there planting. We are out there watering.

212
00:40:09.306 --> 00:40:23.919
Some people you are going to talk to and they are, I mean like it is as if God has done all this work in their life and you walk up and you ask a question and they just start crying and say, tell me how to follow Jesus.

213
00:40:23.919 --> 00:40:36.998
And you are like, wow, should it all be that easy? Because what? Because God is the one who causes the growth. God has prepared that person and they are ready and you are just the recipient of it.

214
00:40:36.998 --> 00:40:48.342
And I think what happens is if you do not plant and you do not water, I do not think God gives you many opportunities to be the one who is involved in seeing the reaping.

215
00:40:48.342 --> 00:41:02.155
And you just kind of think, well, how come that never happens to me? Well, it is because you never got started. And so your job is to pray, God, give me courage because I am going to wimp out. Like I cannot.

216
00:41:02.155 --> 00:41:10.296
I do not think I have ever shared the gospel with anybody that my palms did not perspire. I like boldness. Pray for words.

217
00:41:10.296 --> 00:41:24.776
I do not know what I am going to say, but God give me words to say, a word of encouragement, a word of prayer, a question to ask. Give me the words to say. And finally, that God you would open up doors of opportunity.

218
00:41:24.776 --> 00:41:36.854
And I trust that you are already working. God loves the people that work with you. Jesus died for them. Jesus died for them. Okay. So begin to pray. This is how we apply the method.

219
00:41:36.854 --> 00:41:50.199
Second letter B is inventory your life. Inventory your life in three areas. First of all, number one, your speech. What do you say? Number two, your ethics. How do you do things? What are your values?

220
00:41:50.199 --> 00:41:53.602
Number three is your attitude. It is your attitude.

221
00:41:53.602 --> 00:42:08.482
In Colossians chapter 4 verses 5 and 6, Paul says, "Be wise in the way you act toward outsiders." In other words, your behavior to people who are outside the faith will speak volumes about what it is that you have embraced.

222
00:42:08.482 --> 00:42:22.228
In other words, if Jesus is not changing your life, why would anybody want you to recommend them to him? A great message needs a great messenger in order to be heard. That does not mean a perfect messenger.

223
00:42:22.228 --> 00:42:34.105
What that means is a growing, changing person that is experiencing the grace of God, working at it, living it out imperfectly, laying the groundwork for more and more confidence.

224
00:42:34.105 --> 00:42:48.652
I one time had a police officer, this was probably 20 years ago, tell me, well, you know, in my department, I feel like all the leaders are really unethical. They are really unethical, and I have just had enough of it.

225
00:42:48.652 --> 00:42:59.595
I need to take a stand. I feel like I am going to quit to take a stand. And I just asked him, are they asking you to do anything that is unethical? And he said, no.

226
00:42:59.595 --> 00:43:12.807
And I said, so if you take a stand and quit because you are morally offended by what these other people are doing, who is going to be there to represent the alternative? You know what was happening?

227
00:43:12.807 --> 00:43:21.815
His attitude was so bad. His speech was so sarcastic and cutting that what he had actually done was create an adversarial relationship.

228
00:43:21.815 --> 00:43:34.560
Not because only what they were doing wrong, but because of the way he was responding to what they were doing wrong. Listen folks, when sinners sin, they are just doing their job description.

229
00:43:34.560 --> 00:43:48.906
And we are not the moral police for other people. We are the moral police for ourselves. And we are the proclaimers of freedom to the captive of grace to the sinner of God's love even while people are still sinning.

230
00:43:48.906 --> 00:44:01.451
And too many people act like Pharisees. Oh, look what you are doing wrong. You are doing wrong. You are doing wrong. Well, what would you expect if people do not have the Spirit of Christ?

231
00:44:01.451 --> 00:44:12.061
When you did not have the Spirit of Christ in you, did you have it all together? Of course not. So our attitude, our ethics, our speech make a huge difference.

232
00:44:12.061 --> 00:44:23.004
Letter C, develop relationships. Part of what we are supposed to do is develop relationships. He says in this passage, "Be wise in the way you act toward outsiders.

233
00:44:23.004 --> 00:44:36.550
Make the most of every opportunity." We are supposed to be looking for opportunities to develop relationships. Ask people about what is going on in their life. Start conversations. Be friendly to people.

234
00:44:36.550 --> 00:44:45.758
Build relationships. Invite people over. Do not simply connect with people at work and then as soon as you are done you walk out the door.

235
00:44:45.758 --> 00:44:54.499
We had a very interesting group, they did a survey of Austin leaders a number of years ago and here is what they began to discover.

236
00:44:54.499 --> 00:45:06.643
The majority of Christians in Austin do not even know the Christians that they work with. In fact, the guy who headed up the survey was invited into a board meeting of a corporation.

237
00:45:06.643 --> 00:45:20.522
Walked into the board meeting and saw some people like, oh, you guys you are an elder at this church and you are an elder at this church. And he pulled the two together and said, did you guys know each other?

238
00:45:20.522 --> 00:45:32.133
Yeah, we have been working together for 10 years. Did you all know that you are both elders at churches? And both of them looked at each other said, had no idea. Had no idea.

239
00:45:32.133 --> 00:45:45.011
Two guys sitting at the boardroom together, believers in Jesus Christ, have never developed enough of a conversation with each other to even know. So like I run in, get it done, I run back out.

240
00:45:45.011 --> 00:45:49.748
What about the people behind? Develop some relationships along the way.

241
00:45:49.748 --> 00:45:59.824
Letter D, share your grace story. Share your grace story. Share your grace story. Three aspects of a grace story. So what does a grace story look like?

242
00:45:59.824 --> 00:46:10.834
First of all, it starts with I felt, what you thought and felt before Christ. Here is where I was before Christ. I found, how you came to know Christ as your Savior.

243
00:46:10.834 --> 00:46:21.444
I feel, what you think and feel since coming to Christ. It is your personal story. You say, those sound like some real emotional words. Why are you doing that?

244
00:46:21.444 --> 00:46:31.586
Because your grace story is different than sharing the gospel. We will talk about that just a minute. But this is your story about what happened to you.

245
00:46:31.586 --> 00:46:44.264
Very few people will stop you and tell you I do not want to hear about your own experience. They will let you talk. Now, one of the things I would say is it depends on how long you talk for.

246
00:46:44.264 --> 00:46:58.077
So, you need to have a 30-second story, a three-minute story, and a 10-minute story and know the difference between when to use those. Okay? Get that because you are trying to let them know your grace story.

247
00:46:58.077 --> 00:47:07.018
Letter E, share the gospel message and how one comes to Christ. By this, we are talking about explaining what it means to be a sinner.

248
00:47:07.018 --> 00:47:17.027
Explaining what the judgment or consequences are, explaining what Jesus did for them, explaining how they can know and have a relationship with Jesus.

249
00:47:17.027 --> 00:47:27.503
If you do not know how to do that, we have got all kinds of training to help people. Stop and talk to Nate. Ask him to get you set up. We can get you set up.

250
00:47:27.503 --> 00:47:37.912
You can actually explain the gospel to people in about three or four minutes. In about three or four minutes. And there is a point in time when you do that.

251
00:47:37.912 --> 00:47:49.389
One of the other things I would just encourage you guys to do, most of you at some point in time have learned about an elevator speech. You know what an elevator speech is?

252
00:47:49.389 --> 00:48:04.203
It is the thing you can share, the vision you can share in such a succinct form that from the time a person steps on the elevator with you and goes up to the next floor and gets off, you have got them completely convinced.

253
00:48:04.203 --> 00:48:11.810
And a lot of people when they are starting a company, they will work on that. Like here is what this is all about.

254
00:48:11.810 --> 00:48:26.023
Because you are talking to the venture capital guys, you got to be able to like bump into somebody and within a minute get them hooked. Let me just give you a little elevator speech to start a gospel conversation.

255
00:48:26.023 --> 00:48:33.830
Friend of mine in Miami said he started doing this out on the boardwalk and he has all kinds of gospel conversations.

256
00:48:33.830 --> 00:48:47.776
In talking to people he asked them do they go to church and invariably particularly in Miami he gets a negative reaction. So he has opened it up to let them talk. Do you go to church? Gets a negative reaction.

257
00:48:47.776 --> 00:48:58.786
When they finish talking and people will tell you what they think. He just says this. Well, you know God loves you and he has a plan for your life. Just that simple.

258
00:48:58.786 --> 00:49:04.858
You know God loves you and he has a plan for your life. He gets two reactions. Walked away.

259
00:49:04.858 --> 00:49:19.538
The other reaction he gets is because a person has been moved by the Spirit to know and desire that God does love them, that somebody out there does care for them, and there is a plan. And people will say, how do I know?

260
00:49:19.538 --> 00:49:27.412
What is the plan? And it is easy to talk about the love of God expressed in Jesus Christ as he gave his life for them.

261
00:49:27.412 --> 00:49:38.822
Is there something that you have prepared that you can say like that to move into a conversation about where somebody is at spiritually? You ought to be prepared for that.

262
00:49:38.822 --> 00:49:51.367
Okay, let me wrap up with an image here. Imagine that you got contacted by the CIA this afternoon and they said, you are just the person we need. You know, Russia is raising its ugly head.

263
00:49:51.367 --> 00:50:03.778
Putin is kind of out of control. These things he is doing. We actually need operatives to figure out some kind of cover to go into Russia and spy to figure out what they are doing there.

264
00:50:03.778 --> 00:50:16.456
And so you start thinking to yourself, well, like, what would I do? What would I do? Who could I get? How would I go about doing this? And so you think, well, all the Russians love circuses.

265
00:50:16.456 --> 00:50:20.993
So you recruit a team of operatives that can function like a circus.

266
00:50:20.993 --> 00:50:50.220
